    "result_text": "Green again: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nBoth findings addressed:\n\n**Finding 1 (stale javadoc) \u2014 fixed.** `OwnerMapper.fiscalYear(LocalDate)` no longer references the removed \"membership-number year segment.\" It now states it's the single source of truth used both when `OwnerRestControllerV1.memberIdFor` bakes the FY segment into the member id and when the DTO's `fiscalYear` falls back to the registration date for a legacy record.\n\n**Finding 2 (scattered positional-parsing invariant) \u2014 fixed.** The trailing-width layout now lives in one place: named width constants (`FY_WIDTH`, `HASH8_WIDTH`, `CHK_WIDTH`, `MEMBER_ID_SUFFIX_WIDTH`) plus two decoder helpers, `memberIdRegion(base)` and `memberIdFyDigits(base)`. `memberIdBase`, `toLocality`, and `toFiscalYear` now delegate to these instead of re-deriving the magic `11`/`9` offsets, so the width knowledge is defined once in the class that documents it. (One deviation from the suggested `private` modifier: interface constants can't be `private` \u2014 they're implicitly `public static final`, consistent with the existing `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_TIMEZONE` constants in the same interface; the `private static` decoder *methods* are fine.)",
